@page "/"

<PageTitle>CS 3500</PageTitle>

<h1>Hello TAs, welcome to Sadie & Madi's Spreadsheet!</h1>
<h2> How to use our spreadsheet: </h2>
<ul>
    <li> Start by navigating to the spreadsheet homepage   </li>
    <li> You should start with your focus in A1 with a spreadsheet of 26 columns and 99 rows. This is the max size of a spreadsheet.  </li>
    <li> Cells can be edited by clicking on the contents section of the toolbar.   </li>
    <li> The cell you are "focused" on will be displayed in the toolbar.   </li>
    <li> You can update the contents of a cell by clicking on it.   </li>
    <li> The contents bar will show the original contents a user puts.   </li>
    <li> The value bar will show the evaluation of a cell's contents.   </li>

</ul>

<h2> Issues we had & important bugs to note: </h2>
<ul>
    <li> We were unable to display a useful error message for formula errors inside of a cell itself. There is a simple "ERROR" displayed in the toolbar.   </li>
    <li> Clear has two prompts, one for asserting that the user would like to clear and one for informing the user if there were changes that may be overwritten.  </li>
    <li> We were unable to create a useful load message if the user tries to load an invalid file.   </li>
</ul>

<h2> Additional Features: </h2>
<ul>
    <li> You will notice a "beta" button on our spreadsheet. 
        This will take you to the beginning of our implementation of allowing the user to directly input 
        their contents directly into a cell. </li>
    <li> We were unable to work out some of the visual issues, like the additional boxes that exist around all of the cells.
        Instead of just deleting it we decided to add an additional page so you could look at it without compromising 
        our original spreadsheet. </li>
    <li> We did not work how the toolbar would be worked into this additional feature. </li>
    <li> In order to exit the beta version, instead of reloading the page, simply return Home (this page) and then navigate back to spreadsheet. </li>
</ul>

